<title>SINGAPORE: Fidelity buys 5.18 pct of ABR Holdings.</title>
<headline>Fidelity buys 5.18 pct of ABR Holdings.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foods group ABR Holdings Ltd said on Wednesday two Fidelity mutual funds had acquired 2.31 million shares, or 5.18 percent, of the company's stock.</p>
<p>ABR said in a statement sent to the Stock Exchange of Singapore the shares had been registered in the names of Fidelity Emerging Markets Fund and Fidelity Emerging Markets Portfolio.</p>
<p>The shares had been bought at between Singapore $1.66 and S$2.99 per share. It did not say when the stock was bought.</p>
<p>Fidelity is a U.S. mutual fund based in Boston.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
